+Also called: NeRF Forward Pass, NeRF Forward Pass with Ray Marching and Accumulation, Panoptic-Radiance Field Rendering, Standard NeRF forward, Training Ray Marching
 
 ## Overview
-Training Ray Marching and Integration is the differentiable forward pass that synthesizes a 2D image from a 3D neural radiance field during the optimization loop. It solves the problem of computing gradients for network parameters by approximating the continuous volume rendering integral as a discrete weighted sum, where weights are determined by the probability of a ray terminating at each sample point [S1, S3, S5, S10, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from [NeRF Evaluation and Metric Calculation](3079-nerf-evaluation-and-metric-calculation.md) by enabling stochastic perturbations and adaptive sampling to facilitate gradient-based learning, rather than producing deterministic results for metric computation [S2, S3, S5, S10, unofficial].
+Training Ray Marching and Integration is the differentiable forward pass that synthesizes a 2D image from a 3D neural radiance field during the optimization loop [S1, unofficial][S3][S5, S10, unofficial]. It solves the problem of computing gradients for network parameters by approximating the continuous volume rendering integral as a discrete weighted sum, where weights are determined by the probability of a ray terminating at each sample point [S1, unofficial][S3][S5, S10, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from [NeRF Evaluation and Metric Calculation](3079-nerf-evaluation-and-metric-calculation.md) by enabling stochastic perturbations and adaptive sampling to facilitate gradient-based learning, rather than producing deterministic results for metric computation [S2, unofficial][S3][S5, S10, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method takes camera parameters and a scene representation as input, generates rays, samples 3D points along those rays, queries a neural network for density and color, and integrates the results using alpha compositing.
